{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/215775-mummies-in-rio","id":215775,"title":"Mummies in Rio","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-01T05:34:35-07:00","id":215775,"title":"Mummies in Rio","content":"Partially because I'm going to be running a solo game there soon, and partially because I'm legitimately curious, let's talk about Mummies in Rio de Janeiro and South America. So far in the books I've only seen it come up once, in <i>Eve of Judgment</i>. I get the sense that there's going to be an interesting class divide between the South American<br /> <br /> In a broader sense, I figure that mummies probably came to South America seeking relics, at least during the 16-18th centuries (<i>El Dorado</i> and all that jazz, which will feature prominently in my aforementioned game). What did they find, if anything? Or, more specifically, what do <i>you</i> think they found? El Dorado was never officially found (and debunked in 1804) but that doesn't mean there wasn't some truth to the myth. Or perhaps some enterprising Arisen or Shuankhsen found it, said, &quot;I think I'll be keeping this&quot; and arranged to have it &quot;disproven&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this post came across as rambly. I'm just trying to spur discussion and speculation about this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T06:29:14-07:00","id":215801,"title":"","content":"The Maa-Kep section of Guildhalls has a section on how the Guild operates in each continent. If I remember right, the Maa-Kep in South America have become pretty humanitarian.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe Eve of Judgement makes mention of the fact that there are two classes of Mummy in Rio. Some have been there long before the arrival of Europeans, and their Cults are usually built among the poor segments of the population. The Mummies who arrived with the Europeans, meanwhile, have something of a monopoly on the better off parts of town and don't appreciate &quot;native&quot; Mummies trying to muscle in on their turf.<br /> <br /> So, mid-post I decided to double-check Guildhalls. The Maa-Kep there call themselves &quot;Hall of the Jagged Pyramid&quot;, and they often exploit the widespread mixing of African Orishas and Catholic beliefs to cast Saints as masks for the Judges. And, sure enough, they're a hotbed of Maa-Kep humanists who quietly believe that Irem will never rise again. Their Guildmaster even hopes to create a national economy that doesn't rely on a permanent underclass. All pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> There should be a book on the subject coming out at... some point in the future, I haven't been keeping track. But given that the Arisen secret police in South America seem to have gone native it certainly promises to be a dynamic and fascinating setting. I know that if I were going to delve into heretical research and apotheosis, I'd do it in the area where the people who keep an eye out for that kind of thing are too busy trying to push a social justice agenda among the mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:26:37-07:00","id":215830,"title":"","content":"Cursed Necropolis: Rio appears to still be in it's early stages. I think it'll be awhile.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:48:41-07:00","id":215852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/215775-mummies-in-rio?p=215801#post215801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maa-Kep section of Guildhalls has a section on how the Guild operates in each continent. If I remember right, the Maa-Kep in South America have become pretty humanitarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been a while since I read Guildhalls, and at the time that section didn't jump out at me. Perhaps appropriately, I forgot about it (and also how funny the whole Maa-Kep section is, kudos to the writer). So thanks for bringing that up!<br /> <br /> I like that there's a baked-in class divide between the &quot;natives&quot; and the &quot;colonists&quot;, which should make my solo game more interesting (being as it's set during the 18th century, which means I've got several slave revolts coming up that I'll get to incorporate).<br /> <br /> Now I really want to see the Rio book for the bigger picture look at South America. Its history, especially the history of the &quot;native&quot; mummies, as well as the political climate as it applies to <i>all</i> guilds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T15:25:42-07:00","id":217013,"title":"","content":"I would almost imagine el dorado to be a hotbed of native mummy activity, and is perhaps near a mortal town in which the natives are the force in power (not the europeans). El dorado couldve been a massive tomb/temple structure, filled with relics and mummies. Mesen nebu likely had a potent place in a city of gold, unless you use it as a metaphor (perhaps the &quot;gold&quot; was the spiritual knowledge of the su menent and their Temple). It and the Fountain of Youth are probably the superstars of relics/places in South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}